From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:59:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: OPLUS: list power_now

The OPLUS battery supply has its own property list (oplus_bat_props)
and POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW is not in it, so the power_now value
computed from voltage and current for this variant ("compute power_now
on kaanapali") never reaches sysfs: rehearsal r2z found no power_now
file in /sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat.

Add the property to the OPLUS list. The generic update still asks the
firmware for BATT_POWER_NOW first (its value is only kept for the
dev_dbg comparison line); SuperTurtleDev saw the firmware answer that
request on the same SoC.

Fixes: b9ef24cf2be8 ("power: supply: qcom_battmgr: compute power_now on kaanapali")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 3fb8302226a4..63aa980d5724 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1425,6 +1425,7 @@ static const enum power_supply_property oplus_bat_props[] = {
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
-- 
